right team\n- Spot follow-ups that may need attention\n- Start the day with a shared view of support priorities\n\nChoose the Slack channel that makes the most sense for your team—whether that’s a dedicated support channel, a customer-success workspace, or a team-wide updates channel.\n\n## Get started\n\nConnect Slack from your helpdesk settings, select the channel where you’d like summaries posted, and you’re ready to go.\n\nThe integration is available now for existing customers. Set it up today and make support visibility part of your team’s daily workflow.\n=== END OF TEXT A ===\n\n=== TEXT B ===\n**Never Miss an Open Ticket Again: Daily Summaries in Slack Are Here**\n\nHi there,\n\nWe have news you'll see first thing tomorrow morning — literally.\n\nStarting today, our helpdesk connects with Slack to post a daily summary of your open support tickets right to the channel of your choice. No more tab-switching, digging through dashboards, or asking \"what's still open?\" in standup.\n\nWe built this for busy support teams who live in Slack. Now everyone — from agents to managers to engineering partners — starts the day with the same clear picture.\n\nHere's what your Daily Digest includes:\n\n* Total open tickets, grouped by status and priority\n* Tickets waiting longest and those breaching SLA soon\n* New tickets since yesterday and recently resolved\n* Direct links to jump into any ticket in one click\n\nYou choose the channel (#support-daily, #cs-escalations, you name it) and the time it posts, so it fits how your team already works — whether that's a 9 a.m. triage ritual or an async check-in across time zones.\n\nGetting started takes less than 2 minutes:\n\n1. Go to Settings > Integrations > Slack in your helpdesk admin.\n2. Connect your Slack workspace and pick a channel.\n3. Choose your delivery time and timezone, then hit Save.\n\nThat's it. Your first summary will arrive on the next scheduled run.\n\nThis integration is live now for all existing customer